 contains © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL-1.0","aliases":[],"authors":["Open Landmarks contributors"],"artisticLicense":"CC-BY-4.0","spatialDataLicense":"ODbL-1.0","licenseScope":"CC BY applies to original artistic contributions only; ODbL applies to OSM-derived spatial data. Reference photographs retain their own licenses.","review":{"status":"pending","reviewer":null,"checks":{}},"modelingNotes":["Mapped 19-part plans retain the open internal courts, circular office ring, 20/31 m stepped wings and 68 m central archive tower.","Selected Commons river-front and Eiffel Tower photographs establish the white facade bands, dense rectangular glazing and raised tower crown; glazing uses the project light-blue material instead of photographic black reflections.","Three unheighted named studios lie inside the mapped 10 m interior base; they are not invented as taller volumes.","Named 15 m Studio 104 and Auditorium footprints override the coarse overlapping 20 m front-wing outline; this exposes their lower roofs rather than burying them beneath the parent cap.","The shallow mapped auditorium dome remains structural blue glazing; other wall=no glass roofs are thin coverings rather than full-height solid blocks.","Window bays are original map-scale simplifications at 18 m ring spacing and 6 m tower spacing. Rooftop lettering, equipment and facade posters are omitted."],"source":{"url":"/objects/fc47432f6f3dbb09e5f14610f458cd634837bf41cbe8df1cc26a282ccf3e0b91/source.blend.gz","bytes":216049,"sha256":"fc47432f6f3dbb09e5f14610f458cd634837bf41cbe8df1cc26a282ccf3e0b91"},"spatialSource":{"url":"/objects/609faf6160889d2527d70a9ace722ee198aeacfeb2b7de310e82c733e39da834/spatial-source.json","bytes":42692,"sha256":"609faf6160889d2527d70a9ace722ee198aeacfeb2b7de310e82c733e39da834"},"preview":{"url":"/objects/9fa267967f9e5d31b513bb30f278936e5eec52c5ec0778a5528df106636a5d6b/preview.webp","bytes":10832,"sha256":"9fa267967f9e5d31b513bb30f278936e5eec52c5ec0778a5528df106636a5d6b"},"revision